docs/phase-1-plan.md:11:1. **Secrets in Rails credentials**, production-only file (`config/credentials/production.yml.enc`), keys `schwab.app_key`, `schwab.app_secret`, `mcp.bearer_token`, `anthropic.api_key`, `resend.api_key`, plus Active Record Encryption keys. `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL` and `MEMORY_REPO_PATH` stay in dokku ENV (not secret). The dokku `SCHWAB_APP_KEY`/`SCHWAB_APP_SECRET` vars get unset once the credentials file is on the server. Rotating the MCP token is an edit to the credentials file plus a deploy.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:13:3. **Web login is passwordless magic link**, built on the Rails 8 auth generator with `generates_token_for :magic_link` (15 min, single use). Users are seeded, not self-registered: john@athayde.com and whitney@athayde.com only. No gem. Because a second person can log in, `audit_events.user_id` exists from day one so Phase 2 approvals are attributable. Fallback when email is down: `bin/rails login:link[email]` prints a magic link to the console.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:14:4. **Email via Resend over SMTP**, no gem; API key in credentials. Production login and re-auth depend on it, so Resend DNS is a prerequisite for the first production deploy.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:17:7. **Off-hours cadence** for orders/transactions sync: hourly.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:28:| 1 | `users`, `sessions` | Rails 8 auth generator, password column removed; `email_address` unique. Magic-link tokens via `generates_token_for`, no table. | yes (two seeded users) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:29:| 2 | `schwab_tokens` | `access_token` (encrypted), `refresh_token` (encrypted), `access_expires_at`, `refresh_expires_at` (= `issued_at` + 168 hours, never moved by access refreshes), `issued_at`, `last_refreshed_at`, `last_refresh_error`, `revoked_at`, `scope` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:30:| 3 | `accounts` | `schwab_hash` (Schwab's opaque hashValue, unique), `account_type` enum (taxable/ira, nullable: set by the operator since Schwab only reports CASH or MARGIN), `trading_enabled` bool, `nickname`, `last_synced_at`, `raw` jsonb. A plaintext account number is never a column. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:45:| 18 | `sync_runs` | `feed` enum (accounts, positions, orders, activities, market_hours, memory_repo, snapshots; balances ride with positions), `account_id` (nullable; cursors are per account and feed), `status` (running, succeeded, partial, failed, skipped_token), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `error`, `records_touched`, `unmapped_values` jsonb, `window_from`, `window_to` (captured before the request; the next window starts from it), `gap_from` (set when the computed window start is later than the last success: data Schwab can no longer return) | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:46:| 19 | `agent_runs` | `kind` enum (morning_brief, eod, sunday_review), `status`, `degraded` bool (ran with expired token / stale data), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `tool_turns`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `estimated_cost`, `output_markdown`, `error`, `model` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:48:| 21 | `system_settings` | Singleton row (check constraint `id = 1`): `shadow_mode` bool default true, `manual_halt` bool default false, `manual_halt_reason`, `manual_halt_at`, `sync_paused_reason` (set while token expired) | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:50:Solid Queue / Cache / Cable schemas already generated. Every datetime column is `timestamptz` (adapter default set in an initializer). Schema format is `structure.sql` for the audit triggers; the dump pins Postgres 17 settings, so dokku runs the postgres:17 image. Active Record Encryption: production keys live in `config/credentials/production.yml.enc`; development and test share `config/credentials.yml.enc` (dev keys) with fixed test keys in `config/environments/test.rb`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:58:**Token model (revised after the step 4 counselors review).** Pause state is *derived* from the current token, never written by a failure. `schwab_tokens` gains `revoked_at`; `SchwabToken.current` is the newest by `issued_at, id`; `usable?` = present, not refresh-expired (`issued_at + 168.hours`, elapsed time not calendar days), not revoked. `SchwabToken.issue!(response)` inserts the new row and clears `system_settings.sync_paused_reason` in one transaction, enqueuing `Sync::CatchUpJob` after commit. `SchwabToken#refresh!` takes the row lock, reloads, and returns early if the row is no longer current or was refreshed in the last minute (so two workers cannot double-refresh and a stale row cannot act); it builds the client inside the lock; `access_expires_at` = now + `expires_in` − 60 s; `refresh_token` = response value or the existing one; `refresh_expires_at` is never touched. On `ReauthRequired` it sets `revoked_at` on the current row only, records `last_refresh_error` outside the lock so a rollback cannot lose it, audits `token_refresh_failed`, and sets `sync_paused_reason`. On `ServerError`/`TransportError` it records the error and does nothing else. `ensure_fresh!(margin:)` refreshes proactively when the access token is near expiry, so a 401 is the safety net rather than the norm. `Schwab.client` raises `Schwab::NoUsableToken` rather than letting nil reach a request.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:60:**Token gating.** Only `Sync::TickJob` and the agent jobs are scheduled; everything else is enqueued by them. When `SchwabToken.current` is not usable, the tick job writes one `sync_runs` `skipped_token` row per hour, audits `sync_paused_token_expired` once per episode, and enqueues nothing. No self-re-enqueue, so the queue cannot grow. The re-auth callback (`issue!`) clears the pause, audits `sync_resumed`, and enqueues `Sync::CatchUpJob`, which runs all feeds with windows widened to cover the gap (capped at the 60-day limit). Agent jobs run degraded rather than wait: `degraded: true`, the prompt states the token is unusable and every number carries its as-of time, the email subject is prefixed, and the token status line sits at the top of every brief so a dead nag path is still visible daily. Snapshots are not written for days without a fresh balance.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:62:**Re-auth flow.** `SchwabController#authorize` (login required) stores a random `state` with a timestamp in the session and redirects to the authorize URL. `#callback` (login required; an unauthenticated hit is rejected without storing a return-to URL, so the code never lands in the session) reads and deletes the pending state; no pending state renders "nothing pending, start again" with no audit; a mismatch audits `re_auth_failed` as CSRF; `params[:error]` (user cancelled) renders the failure without calling the token endpoint. On success: `exchange_code`, then `/accounts/accountNumbers` must overlap the known `accounts` hashes (first auth accepts anything) or the token is not made current and `re_auth_failed` is audited; then `issue!`, audit `re_auth_succeeded`, and **redirect** to a clean success page so a browser refresh cannot resubmit the single-use code. A failed exchange never writes to `schwab_tokens`. The retry link goes to `authorize`. `code`, `state`, and `session` join `filter_parameters`. The callback URL comes only from `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, never from the request. `fake_authorize` 404s unless the adapter is fake and the environment is not production, and `?fail=1` redirects with a bad code for Playwright.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:64:**Health and nags.** `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` runs 08:00 and 20:00 ET. Nag when: no usable token (absent, revoked, or expired), sent at every run; or the 24-hour warning, sent once per token row (deduped on token id in the audit data). Monday/Tuesday escalation fires when `SchwabToken.current.issued_at` is before the most recent Sunday 18:00 ET, which is the PRD's literal "the Sunday re-auth hasn't happened"; no buffer, no comparison against the coming Sunday. Cron strings carry `America/New_York` explicitly. The refresh task gets a higher queue priority than sync.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:68:| `Schwab::RefreshAccessTokenJob` | every 25 min, high priority | `SchwabToken.current&.refresh!`; no-op when there is no usable token |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:69:| `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` | daily 08:00 + 20:00 | See "Health and nags" above. Audits `token_nag_sent` with the token id and reason. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:70:| `Sync::TickJob` | every 5 min | Sole scheduled sync entry point. Refreshes `market_days` for today (New York) plus 7 days when missing or `source: fallback` (one call per date; a market-hours failure never aborts the tick). Due checks compare against the last *started* run per account and feed with 1-minute slack, and a `running` run is never due; jobs also declare Solid Queue `limits_concurrency` keyed on account and feed so backlog cannot double-enqueue. Cadences apply to trading-enabled accounts: positions (15 min inside the session window pre-market through post-market, 60 min otherwise), orders and activities (5 min inside, 60 outside); read-only accounts sync hourly. `Snapshots::DailyJob` once per market day after `regular_closes_at` + 20 min, only when that day's calendar row came from Schwab. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:71:| `Sync::AccountsJob` | daily 06:05, after every re-auth | `/accounts/accountNumbers` only; upsert by `schwab_hash`. New accounts land with `trading_enabled: false` and no `account_type`; the system screen shows accounts needing operator setup |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:84:| `Agent::SundayReviewJob` | Sunday 18:00 | Phase 1 stub, no API call: re-auth link, token age, sync health, job failures, setup stats table |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:86:**Sync runs.** `SyncRun.record(feed, account:, window:)` wraps every feed: creates the row, captures `window_to` before the request, rescues `NoUsableToken`, `AuthError`, and `ReauthRequired` into `skipped_token`, rescues other `Schwab::Error` into `failed`, counts quarantined records into `partial` with `unmapped_values` (raw type, description, subAccount, sign, item shape), and stamps `records_touched`. `partial` advances the cursor; `failed` does not. A cash-affecting `other` activity makes the run `partial`, never a quiet success.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:92:**Market calendar.** `MarketDay.for(date)` reads the row or fetches it (source schwab). When the token is unusable or the call fails it writes a weekday-open 9:30 to 16:00 row with `source: fallback`, which drives cadence only: snapshots and market-day briefs require a Schwab-sourced row, and fallback rows are re-fetched on every tick until they flip. "Today" is computed in America/New_York.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:105:| `get_account_health` | Equity, settled/unsettled cash, drawdown from HWM (index-based), unprotected count, token status and age, last sync per feed, shadow mode, halt state, sync pause reason |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:106:| `get_quotes(symbols)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/quotes`, cached 2 min in Solid Cache, each quote stamped with fetched_at; when the token is expired returns the cached value with `stale: true` or an explicit unavailable error |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:107:| `get_price_history(symbol, range)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/pricehistory`, cached 5 min |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:114:**MCP server:** `POST /mcp` (Streamable HTTP, JSON-RPC 2.0). `McpAuth` extracts a bearer from `Authorization` and compares with `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`; 401 renders a plain "MCP auth failed" page (Playwright target). See decision 0.8 for the OAuth fallback.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:116:**Scheduled runtime:** `Agent::Run` wraps one Messages API conversation: system prompt = memory repo markdown files + setup stats + token health + as-of timestamps; tools = scheduled-allowed registry; hard cap `MAX_TOOL_TURNS = 12`; result stored in `agent_runs` and emailed via `BriefMailer`. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`. The morning-brief prompt states that earnings and economic-calendar data are unavailable in Phase 1 and must not be inferred. Morning brief and EOD are real; Sunday review stub does not call the API.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:164:- `equity` = the latest balance at or after the regular close on that day, else the day's latest balance, else **no snapshot** (a stale balance is never smeared across days). The first snapshot is the first day with positive equity, with return 0 and index 1.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:178:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner (healthy / expiring / expired / halted), equity + day change, open risk with unprotected count, settled/unsettled cash, positions list with distance-to-stop as the primary number and inline `unprotected` where applicable, "N trades need review" callout, pending proposals count (0), staleness stamps on every number, empty state before first sync |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:183:| Login | `/session/new` → email → `/session/magic/:token` | Passwordless; unknown emails get the same "check your inbox" response |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:187:Banner precedence: halted > expired > expiring > healthy. Halted in Phase 1 comes only from `system_settings.manual_halt`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:193:- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:194:- **VCR cassettes** in `spec/cassettes`, recorded against Schwab only once the app is Ready For Use, with a scrubber that replaces bearer tokens, refresh tokens, and account hash values before write. Until then, cassettes are hand-built from community-client response shapes and marked `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:195:- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:196:- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): dashboard in four banner states via a test-env-only `/playwright/scenarios/:name` reseed route, MCP 401 page, re-auth success and failure (FakeClient scripted), trade review flow.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:197:- **`bin/ci`**: Rails 8.1 `ActiveSupport::ContinuousIntegration` with steps in `config/ci.rb`, the pattern borrowed from Patchvault. Kickoff order: rubocop → rspec → brakeman (strict, warnings fail) → `bin/importmap audit` → `bundle exec bundle-audit check --update` → Playwright (`bin/playwright`, which boots a test-env server with the FakeClient, runs `npx playwright test`, and tears down). Fails on the first red step.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:212:1. Tooling: RSpec, rubocop config, brakeman, bundler-audit, `bin/ci` (without Playwright), authentication generator adapted to magic link, AR encryption keys, credentials layout, crest in the layout.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:215:4. OAuth controller + token model + refresh job + token health job + re-auth pages + pause/catch-up + audit events.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:218:7. Dashboard, system health, trade screens; Playwright added to `bin/ci`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:244:- Refresh token expiry is 7 days from issuance and is not extended by access-token refreshes.

