<!-- ============ FLOW 1: DASHBOARD ============ -->
<h2>Flow 1 — Dashboard, banner states</h2>
<p class="flowdesc">Glance screen. One banner max. Distance-to-stop is the primary per-position number; P&amp;L is secondary.</p>

<div class="row">

  <div class="cell">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>Dashboard</b><span>live · 10:04a</span></div>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:18px; margin:6px 0 10px;">
        <div><div class="num">$10,240</div><div class="lbl">Equity · +0.6% today</div></div>
        <div><div class="num">2.4%</div><div class="lbl">Open risk</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Settled / unsettled</span><b>$2,110 / $980</b></div>
      <div class="sec">Positions</div>
      <div class="pos"><div class="top"><span>XYZ · 40</span><span>4.4% to stop</span></div><div class="sub"><span>in @ 51.18</span><span>+$38</span></div></div>
      <div class="pos"><div class="top"><span>DEF · 15</span><span>1.1% to stop</span></div><div class="sub"><span>in @ 88.02</span><span>−$21</span></div></div>
      <div class="kv" style="margin-top:8px;"><span>Pending proposals</span><b>1 →</b></div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">1a · Healthy</p>
    <p class="note">No banner. DEF's 1.1%-to-stop is the loudest number on screen by design.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cell">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>Dashboard</b><span>paused</span></div>
      <div class="banner"><b>Halted:</b> daily loss −2.1% tripped 11:14a. New entries resume tomorrow. Exits remain available.</div>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:18px; margin:6px 0 10px;">
        <div><div class="num">$9,905</div><div class="lbl">Equity · −2.1% today</div></div>
        <div><div class="num">1.0%</div><div class="lbl">Open risk</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sec">Positions</div>
      <div class="pos"><div class="top"><span>XYZ · 40</span><span>3.0% to stop</span></div><div class="sub"><span>in @ 51.18</span><span>−$64</span></div></div>
      <a class="btn disabled">New proposal (halted)</a>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">1b · Halted</p>
    <p class="note">Banner names the rule and the reset time. Entry points disabled, exits untouched. Rule editor also locks.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cell">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>Dashboard</b><span>read-only</span></div>
      <div class="banner"><b>Token expired.</b> Sync paused Sun 6:12p. Re-auth to resume.</div>
      <a class="btn primary">Re-authenticate with Schwab</a>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:18px; margin:10px 0;">
        <div><div class="num">$10,180</div><div class="lbl">Equity · as of Sun 6:12p</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pos"><div class="top"><span>XYZ · 40</span><span>as of Sun 6:12p</span></div><div class="sub"><span>every number carries its age</span><span></span></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">1c · Token expired</p>
    <p class="note">Single call to action. All data stamped stale. App is read-only for anything needing fresh Schwab data.</p>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- ============ FLOW 3 + 4 ============ -->
<h2>Flows 3 &amp; 4 — Manual proposal · Journal quick entry</h2>
<p class="flowdesc">Left: the form computes collar and size live as the stop is typed. Right: the 30-second phone task.</p>

<div class="row">

  <div class="cell">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>New proposal</b><span>you</span></div>
      <div class="field">Symbol — QRS · 18.42 live</div>
      <div class="field">Entry — 18.45</div>
      <div class="field">Stop — 17.20 ▍</div>
      <div class="collar"><div class="track"><div class="band"></div><div class="dot" style="left:52%"></div></div><div class="ends"><span>16.90</span><span>17.80</span></div></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Size (from 1% risk rule)</span><b>81 shares</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Position value</span><b>$1,494</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Settled cash check</span><b>ok</b></div>
      <div class="field">Target — optional</div>
      <div class="field">Setup — pick list</div>
      <a class="btn primary">Create proposal</a>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">3 · Manual proposal</p>
    <p class="note">Collar band + dot update per keystroke on stop. Size is computed, not typed. Submits into the same Flow-2 pipeline.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cell">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>Trade #67 · XYZ</b><span>closed +1.8R</span></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Setup</span><b>breakout-A</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Planned / actual stop</span><b>48.90 / 48.90</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Entry → exit</span><b>51.18 → 55.31</b></div>
      <div class="sec">Post-mortem (one line)</div>
      <div class="field">What actually happened…</div>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; margin-top:8px;">
        <a class="btn" style="margin:0;">Followed setup</a>
        <a class="btn" style="margin:0;">Improvised</a>
      </div>
      <a class="btn primary">Save</a>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">4 · Journal entry</p>
    <p class="note">Two inputs total. Everything else read-only. +1.8R and −1R get identical visual treatment.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cell">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>Proposals</b><span>queue</span></div>
      <div class="empty">Nothing waiting on you.<br>Next scheduled brief: 4:30p.</div>
      <div class="sec">Recent</div>
      <div class="kv"><span>#241 XYZ · filled</span><b>10:03a</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>#240 DEF · rejected</span><b>yesterday</b></div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">Queue · empty state</p>
    <p class="note">Empty is the normal state; it should feel calm, not broken. Recent history keeps the screen useful.</p>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- ============ FLOW 5 + 8 ============ -->
<h2>Flows 5 &amp; 8 — Edge review (desktop) · System health</h2>
<p class="flowdesc">Edge review is the Sunday screen and can assume desktop width. Health is the ops page with the kill switch.</p>

<div class="row">

  <div class="cell wide">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>Edge review</b><span>Sun 8/16 · trailing 20 per setup</span></div>
      <table class="wt">
        <tr><th>Setup</th><th>N</th><th>Win%</th><th>Avg R</th><th>Expectancy</th><th></th></tr>
        <tr><td>breakout-A</td><td>14</td><td>57%</td><td>+0.62</td><td>+0.35R</td><td>active</td></tr>
        <tr><td>pullback-B</td><td>11</td><td>45%</td><td>+0.20</td><td>+0.09R</td><td>active</td></tr>
        <tr class="flag"><td>gap-fade-C</td><td>9</td><td>22%</td><td>−0.48</td><td>−0.31R ⚑</td><td><a class="btn ghost" style="display:inline-block; width:auto; padding:2px 8px; margin:0;">Deactivate…</a></td></tr>
      </table>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px;">Deactivate confirm states the effect: "Agent stops proposing gap-fade-C." Small N gets an insufficient-sample mark rather than a verdict.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">5 · Edge review</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cell">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hd"><b>System</b><span>health</span></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Refresh token age</span><b>4d 02h / 7d</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Next re-auth</span><b>Sun (email)</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Positions sync</span><b>2m ago</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Transactions sync</span><b>4m ago</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>Job failures (7d)</span><b>0</b></div>
      <div class="kv"><span>API spend (Aug)</span><b>$6.40</b></div>
      <a class="btn">Pause system…</a>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">8 · Health + kill switch</p>
    <p class="note">Pause stops proposal creation and submission. Unpause requires typed confirmation.</p>
  </div>

</div>

<p class="footer-note">Not wireframed yet (lower stakes, design directly): journal browser, watchlist, risk-rule editor with effect preview, re-auth success/failure, pre-first-sync empty states. Open design questions these frames surface: (1) what the deliberate confirm on Approve physically is; (2) whether the collar band is a horizontal track (as here) or plotted on a mini price axis; (3) whether the halted state should mute the whole palette or just banner it.</p>

</body>
</html>

